components.responsibility:
Package tests:
- the Send/OwnerInbox round trip;
- Send to a draft report's id returns ErrNoTarget and writes 0 rows;
- Send with a refused body returns ErrBadBody and runs no SQL;
- OwnerInbox order is newest first, and it returns only that report's rows.

Migration test: copy TestCommentsMigrationFromV2AndV3's shape. A database populated at user_version 4 (a user, a published report, a comment, a vote) is opened by the current binary. The result must be user_version == newestVersion, PRAGMA foreign_key_check empty, and the v4 rows intact. Then a fresh database opened at each earlier version from 1 to 4 must reach the same state.

key_decisions.decision:
Migration 0005 lands the epic's whole schema:
- feedback: id AUTOINCREMENT; report_id → reports(id) ON DELETE CASCADE; github_id → users(github_id) with no action; body CHECK(length>0); created_at; STRICT;
- feedback_replies: id AUTOINCREMENT; feedback_id → feedback(id) ON DELETE CASCADE; body; created_at; STRICT; with no author column;
- the indexes (report_id, id) and (feedback_id, id).

Four name fences, the only seams this design adds:
- only internal/feedback names the feedback tables in SQL;
- only admin.go calls Owner(Inbox|Reply)*;
- only reader.go calls SenderThreads;
- internal/feedback never opens a transaction.
Each gets one fire row and one quiet row in the corpus, and nothing more.

SC-017's shape is settled here:
- the reply route is an adminRoutes row whose handler, in admin.go, checks canonicalID, then OwnerReplyTarget, then parses the body, then calls OwnerReply;
- SenderThreads is read in renderReader only for a signed-in non-owner on stateFound, and a read error becomes stateUnavailable;
- the sender's thread is drawn after the form's action.
Blocked senders are left to SC-021: Send stores them, and nothing marks them yet.

proposals.note:
Adopted from practice:
- the separate table and package;
- the single 0005 that includes feedback_replies;
- the #feedback fragment for success and signed out alike;
- the postFeedback and SenderThreads names;
- senders kept distinct from the observers;
- TestFeedbackFollowsReportLifecycle pinning the two-hop cascade;
- running the finish test on a scratch copy and expecting exactly the reply failure.
Its over_engineering_flag was honoured: no workflow states, notifications, paging or rate limit. Its risk about tests pinning user_version 4 was checked and does not apply: the store tests derive the version through newestVersion.

Adopted from crossdomain:
- the Owner* names for the owner-only read and the reply write, with their fence;
- no row id to non-owners (the Sent and Reply types have no ID);
- the two-world comment-id storage-channel subtest;
- reply-target lookup before the body is parsed;
- SenderThreads skipped for the owner.
Rejected:
- the 0006 replies migration, which leaned on an SC-017 spike that will not exist and risked a number collision;
- the #feedback-sent :target confirmation;
- the name Mine, because a `.Mine` fence would hit votes.PublicView.Mine;
- making the nonvoter observer a sender, which SC-017's permitted sink would break.

cases.shape:
body shapes:
- refused: empty, whitespace only, 5001 runes, a NUL, DEL, U+0085, invalid UTF-8, no body field, two body fields, body only in the query string, form over 64 KiB;
- accepted: exactly 5000 runes, CRLF and lone CR, multi-line text, literal <script>x</script>

three failures:
- the session lookup fails (DROP TABLE sessions), with a live cookie and with an unknown 43-character cookie;
- the feedback write fails (ALTER TABLE feedback RENAME TO feedback_gone);
- the owner's inbox read fails

odd spellings and methods:
- GET, HEAD and PUT on /reports/x/feedback;
- a trailing slash and /extra;
- POST /reports/feedback (a report slugged 'feedback');
- //reports/x/feedback and /reports/x/../y/feedback;
- an anonymous POST to a draft x against an unknown x

list shapes:
- a report with no feedback;
- one with several messages from two senders;
- a sender with an avatar and one without;
- feedback on another report;
- a draft report with feedback;
- 2 dislikes cast

outside_claims.claim:
The E-005 finish test does the following:
- sends feedback as POST /reports/<slug>/feedback with one 'body' field;
- reads messages only from elements whose id fully matches feedback-\d+;
- requires the raw text '/reports/<slug>/feedback' before the sender's own message and the reply text;
- requires exactly one number beside a dislike label on the admin page;
- follows only same-host redirects and pins neither the 303 nor any fragment;
- also POSTs /admin/feedback/<n>/reply with one 'body' field;
- sets HBAND_TRUSTED_PROXIES, which config ignores.

epic_parts.builds:
This slice builds:
- migration 0005, both tables and indexes;
- internal/feedback with New, Send, OwnerInbox, Message, ErrBadBody and ErrNoTarget;
- postFeedback and its router line, and the app field;
- feedback.html with three branches, included in report.html, plus the site.css selector widening;
- the inbox section in admin_report.html, with adminData.Feedback and the OwnerInbox call in adminReport;
- the four architecture rules with their corpus rows;
- the tests listed in `cases`.

Tests show it: TestFeedbackSend, TestFeedbackRefusedSenders, TestFeedbackBodies, TestFeedbackHiddenReports, TestFeedbackStoreFailure, TestFeedbackDoesNotInterfere (other readers, sender's own pages, comment ids), TestFeedbackFollowsReportLifecycle, TestFeedbackMigration*, TestReaderPathVariants, TestFeedbackBox, TestReaderPagesShareOneLayout and TestFeedbackOwnerList all pass. The scratch run of the E-005 finish test fails only with 'the admin view offers no reply to the feedback'.
